codex
- **Check that cannot fail**: lines 131-132. Input page `<html><body><span id="x">--</span><span id="x">--</span></body></html>` with object `{"x":"ok","render":[{"block":"text","slot":"x","path":"x"}]}`. Consequence: `count=1` caps `n` at 1, so duplicate matching slots are not detected and one placeholder remains.

- **Idempotency guard satisfied by own marker**: line 139. Input page `<html><body><!-- projector-build-stamp --><span id="x">--</span></body></html>` with object `{"x":"ok","render":[{"block":"text","slot":"x","path":"x"}]}`. Consequence: `STAMP_ID in out` is true, line 140 replaces no `<div>`, and the page can be written without a real provenance stamp.

- **Instrument reading a different copy / wrapper status**: lines 190-191. Input: run `python F:\rapidmeta-ssot-shell\scripts\project_topic_page.py page.html obj.json --apply` from a non-git directory, with otherwise valid repo-relative files. Consequence: failed `git rev-parse` is ignored and a successful wrapper exit can stamp `UNKNOWN` instead of the repo commit.

- **Selector keyed to a form it does not handle**: lines 151 and 166. Input page `<html><SCRIPT>const s="</body>";</SCRIPT><span id="x">--</span></html>` with object `{"x":"ok","render":[{"block":"text","slot":"x","path":"x"}]}`. Consequence: uppercase `<SCRIPT>` is not recognized, so the stamp can be inserted inside JavaScript and the guard misses it.

- **CRLF/LF text comparison**: line 161. Input CRLF page `<html>\r\n<body>\r\n<span id="x">--</span>\r\n</body>\r\n</html>\r\n` with object value `"a\nb"`. Consequence: the check compares only CRLF counts, so it accepts newly introduced bare-LF line endings.

- **Probe keyed to string a fix removes**: lines 121-122. Input: apply once to `<span id="x">--</span>` with object `{"x":"ok","render":[{"block":"text","slot":"x","path":"x"}]}`, then run the same command again. Consequence: success removes `--`, making the rerun refuse instead of verifying the projected value.

- **Merged-cell/off-by-one tabulation**: none found in this file.
- **Zero conflated with absent**: none proven.
- **Negation dropped**: none found.
